  "terms": "# Terms\n\nBy participating, teams agree to the challenge rules and dataset licence published by the organizers. Hidden ground truth, leaked evaluation material, manual truth-based correction, and unauthorized redistribution of challenge data are prohibited.",
  "pages": [
    {
      "id": 84269,
      "title": "Overview",
      "content": "# LiDAR-Visual-Inertial SLAM\n\nThis is the independent LiDAR-visual-inertial track of the Multi-Sensor LiDAR SLAM Challenge 2026. Participants process the two released scenes locally and submit estimated trajectories only. Reliable ground truth and its timestamps remain private on Codabench.\n\nBoth `scene_0001` and `scene_0002` are required. Completion has no hard threshold; missing trajectory coverage reduces AUC recall and the final score.\n\nThe dataset was recorded with an Airy LiDAR and its built-in IMU plus the front-left and front-right Seeker fisheye cameras. The following images are route-shape references only and contain no ground truth.\n\n![Scene 1 trajectory reference](images/scene_0001_trajectory_reference.png)\n\n![Scene 2 trajectory reference](images/scene_0002_trajectory_reference.png)",
      "index": 0
    },
    {
      "id": 84270,
      "title": "Submission",
      "content": "# Submission format\n\nUpload a ZIP whose root contains `README.md` and `trajectories/scene_0001.txt` plus `trajectories/scene_0002.txt`. Each trajectory uses TUM rows:\n\n```text\ntimestamp tx ty tz qx qy qz qw\n```\n\nTimestamps must be strictly increasing. Values must be finite and quaternions must be non-zero. There is no submission-count limit. Only the most recent valid submission is ranked.",
      "index": 1
    },
    {
      "id": 84271,
      "title": "Evaluation",
      "content": "# Evaluation\n\nScoring uses EVO time synchronization and one no-scale SE(3) alignment per scene against the private reference trajectory. Completion has no hard threshold and is published; missing pose pairs reduce AUC recall. Evaluation timestamps and ground truth are not published.\n\nATE is EVO translational APE RMSE. AUC uses EVO one-frame translational RPE and the F1-AUC protocol. RTE is the RMSE of EVO translational RPE normalized at 1 m, 5 m, and 10 m. Aggregate and per-scene RTE@1m, RTE@5m, and RTE@10m are all published alongside the combined RTE. Gaps over 0.3 s are never crossed.\n\nAUC and RTE use aligned world-frame positions with identity orientations, so a fixed participant body-axis convention does not affect translation scores. Every scene uses one scene-level SE(3) alignment.\n\nThe total score is `100 * (0.40 * AUC + 0.40 * exp(-ATE / tau_ate) + 0.20 * exp(-RTE / tau_rte))`. Reference result is the published reference: its aggregate ATE and RTE define `tau_ate` and `tau_rte` after the final scorer is frozen.\n\nResults publish the total score, aggregate and per-scene AUC/ATE/combined RTE/RTE@1m/RTE@5m/RTE@10m, normalized score components, completion, and match counts. Per-timestamp errors, associations, alignment transforms, and ground truth remain private.",
      "index": 2
    }
  ],
